            <ArticleTitle>Survival after spontaneous primary left main coronary artery dissection. Acute surgical intervention with the Jarvik 7-70 artificial heart.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>786-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous primary dissection of a coronary artery is extremely rare, and when it involves the left main trunk the outcome is catastrophic. A 41-year-old woman who survived such a dissection and resultant myocardial infarct with cardiogenic shock is reported here. The patient required a Jarvik 7-70 artificial heart to sustain life until an orthotopic cardiac transplant was performed, and she is now alive and well.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
